This test case models a liquid-cooled cold plate beneath a power-electronics or processor package, where a hotspot moves across the chip as the workload shifts,
and coolant flowing through an internal channel carries the heat away 

The testcase has been modeled as : Full 2D Finite Volume simulation of the transient, conjugate extended-Graetz problem:
thermally developing, hydrodynamically fully developed laminar channel flow with wall conduction and a moving Gaussian wall heat flux.

There is an Energy Balance Check to  ensure no unwanted heat source or sink inside the domain.
